  "c9269817b50682fd8160dbfba10968ca81bdc87d9ea58fc2e25a42c6adf0e5a1": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Functional ovarian cyst is unlikely given its persistence and large size over two years — “The patient observed a gradual abdominal enlargement for two two years before hospitalization.”\n2. Germ cell tumor (e.g., yolk sac tumor, dysgerminoma) is less probable with normal AFP and β-hCG levels — “alpha-fetoprotein was 4.54 ng/mL... B-HCG was <0.200 mIU/mL.”\n3. Epithelial ovarian carcinoma is unlikely because CA-125 was within normal range and imaging showed no solid components — “CA-125 was 23.1 U/mL (N max: 35 U/mL)” and “there were no visible partitions or solid elements.”\n4. Mucinous cystadenoma is less consistent with a simple thin-walled unilocular appearance without septations — “the walls of the lesion were 1.5 mm thick, and there were no visible partitions or solid elements.”\n5. Serous cystadenoma was suggested intraoperatively, but the presence of a significant fibrous stromal component on final histology reclassified the lesion — “Intraoperative histopathology revealed a serous cystadenoma... the final histopathologic examination revealed ovarian cystadenofibroma.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n- The patient presents with a large, fluid-filled ovarian tumor with a thin wall and no septations or solid components, which is suggestive of a benign ovarian cystadenoma. The tumor markers are mostly within normal limits, which further supports a benign diagnosis.\n- The patient presents with a large, fluid-filled ovarian tumor with a thin wall and no septations or solid components, which is suggestive of a mucinous cystadenoma. The tumor markers are mostly within normal limits, which further supports a benign diagnosis.\n- The patient's clinical presentation and imaging findings are also consistent with a serous ovarian cystadenoma, which is another type of benign ovarian tumor. The absence of solid components and the thin wall of the tumor make a malignant diagnosis less likely.\n\nA