  "df15a33baf8440a25aedcf398696c7c0275817705f520034491eed558963c95d": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Primary colorectal adenocarcinoma — “primary colorectal tumours tend to demonstrate the opposite pattern being positive for CDX2 and negative for TTF1…”\n2. Primary gastrointestinal neuroendocrine tumour — “Although neuroendocrine tumours can arise in any body region 95% of all small cell carcinomas are lung origin…”\n3. Metastatic Merkel cell carcinoma — “Metastatic Merkel cell carcinoma is considered less likely as there is no cytoplasmic CK20 staining.”\n4. Metastatic small cell carcinoma of lung — “positive immunostaining for TTF1 with negative staining for Caudal-type Homeobox 2 (CDX2) lead us to suspect a lung origin tumour…”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n- Diagnosis: Perforated Appendicitis with Peritonitis\n  Evidence: The patient presented with acute right lower-quadrant abdominal pain, fever, hypotension, and tachycardia, and imaging showed a perforated appendix with surrounding fat stranding and peritonism, which are classic signs of perforated appendicitis with peritonitis.\n- Diagnosis: Colorectal Cancer\n  Evidence: The patient had a history of prostate cancer and presented with a thickened, woody sigmoid colon, mural thickening of the cecum and sigmoid colon, and lymphadenopathy, which are suspicious for colorectal cancer. The subtotal colectomy with end ileostomy also suggests a possible malignancy.\n\nFor each groundtruth statement, consider potential matches:\n\nStatement 1 (Primary colorectal adenocarcinoma): The predicted \"Colorectal Cancer\" evidence mentions clinical and imaging findings but does not reference CDX2, TTF1, or immunohistochemistry. No match. Pros: Both involve colorectal cancer. Cons: The groundtruth statement is specifically about immunohistochemical pattern (CDX2+/TTF1-), while predicted evidence is about clinical presentation and imaging. Not equivalent justification. No match.\n\nStatement 2 (Primary gastrointestinal neuroendocrine tumour): Predicted reasons do not mention neuroendocrine tumour, small cell carcinoma, or any related markers. No match.\n\nStatement 3 (Metastatic Merkel cell carcinoma): Predicted reasons do not mention Merkel cell carcinoma, CK20, or any related findings. No match.\n\nStatement 4 (Metastatic small cell carcinoma of lung): Predicted reasons do not mention TTF1, CDX2, or lung origin. No match.\n\nSummary: No matching statements exist between groundtruth and predicted diagnostic reasons. All groundtruth statements have zero matches.\n\nJSON output:\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}",
    "prompt_id": "mcr.reasoning_recall"
  },
