  "ff4da219d976377652b644d4051209a652898358c4b665ddf58ffa2e4c43a4d2": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Cavernous angioma was initially suspected based on imaging — “suggesting the presence of a cavernous angioma.”\n2. Meningeal sarcoma with angiosarcomatous features was favored by pathology — “suggestive of meningeal sarcoma with angiosarcomatous features, ultimately assessed as a malignant endothelial cell sarcoma/AS.”\n3. Gliosarcoma was considered given the biphasic pattern of glial and mesenchymal differentiation — “Gliosarcoma ... was also considered. Further molecular analysis did not detect the presence of O6-methylguanine-DNA methyltransferase promoter methylation.”\n4. Metastatic malignancy was entertained due to a solitary pulmonary nodule on PET — “a concurrent PET scan showed a solitary pulmonary nodule assessed to be an infectious process or a malignancy.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n- \"The patient's histopathological examination demonstrated spindle cells forming masses with branching ectatic vasculature, focal collagenous regions, and up to 20 mitoses per ten high-power fields. Immunohistochemical studies showed strong immunoreactivity for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1, which are consistent with hemangiopericytoma.\"\n- \"The patient's histopathological examination demonstrated spindle cells forming masses with branching ectatic vasculature, focal collagenous regions, and up to 20 mitoses per ten high-power fields. Immunohistochemical studies showed strong immunoreactivity for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1, which are characteristic of hemangiopericytoma.\"\n- \"The patient's imaging and histopathological findings, including a left tentorial extra-axial enhancing mass with adjacent parenchymal hemorrhage and spindle cells forming masses with branching ectatic vasculature, are consistent with Hemangiopericytoma. The strong immunoreactivity for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1 also supports this diagnosis.\"\n- \"The histopathological examination showing spindle cells with branching ectatic vasculature, focal collagenous regions, and high mitotic activity, combined with immunohistochemical positivity for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1, is consistent with a diagnosis of hemangiopericytoma, a type of vascular tumor.\"\n- \"The patient's histopathological findings, including spindle cells forming masses with focal collagenous regions and strong immunoreactivity for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1, are also consistent with Solitary Fibrous Tumor. However, the presence of up to 20 mitoses per ten high-power fields and the aggressive behavior of the tumor, as evidenced by its invasion of the falx cerebri and adjacent cortex, are more suggestive of Hemangiopericytoma.\"\n- \"The tumor's immunohistochemical profile, including strong staining for CD31, CD99, and Fli-1, and negative staining for CD34, EMA, desmin, and Bcl-2, is also compatible with a solitary fibrous tumor, although the presence of high mitotic activity and the specific vascular pattern may lean more towards hemangiopericytoma.\"\n\nNow, for each groundtruth statement, consider potential matches:\n\nStatement 1: Cavernous angioma initially suspected based on imaging.\n- Predicted statements: None mention cavernous angioma, imaging suspicion, or any alternative diagnosis. All focus on hemangiopericytoma/solitary fibrous tumor histology. No match.\n\nStatement 2: Meningeal sarcoma with angiosarcomatous features favored by pathology.\n- Predicted statements: No mention of meningeal sarcoma, angiosarcomatous features, or malignant endothelial cell sarcoma. No match.\n\nStatement 3: Gliosarcoma considered due to biphasic pattern.\n- Predicted statements: No mention of gliosarcoma, biphasic pattern of glial and mesenchymal differentiation, or MGMT methylation. No match.\n\nStatement 4: Metastatic malignancy entertained due to solitary pulmonary nodule.\n- Predicted statements: No mention of metastatic malignancy, solitary pulmonary nodule, PET scan, or infectious process. No match.\n\nThus, no predicted statements match any groundtruth statement.\n\nSummary: All groundtruth statements have zero matching predicted statements.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n\n<output>\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n</output>",
    "prompt_id": "mcr.reasoning_recall"
  },
